R49	Addressee Arg1:T35 Arg2:T36	
T37	Quotation 5194 5388	"I been to the circus three or four times-- lots of times. Church ain't shucks to a circus. There's things going on at a circus all the time. I'm going to be a clown in a circus when I grow up."
T38	Quotation 5389 5457	"Oh, are you! That will be nice. They're so lovely, all spotted up."
T39	Quotation 5458 5580	"Yes, that's so. And they get slathers of money-- most a dollar a day, Ben Rogers says. Say, Becky, was you ever engaged?"
T40	Quotation 5581 5595	"What's that?"
T41	Quotation 5596 5625	"Why, engaged to be married."
T42	Quotation 5626 5631	"No."
T43	Quotation 5632 5652	"Would you like to?"
T44	Quotation 5653 5698	"I reckon so. I don't know. What is it like?"
T45	Quotation 5699 5865	"Like? Why it ain't like anything. You only just tell a boy you won't ever have anybody but him, ever ever ever, and then you kiss and that's all. Anybody can do it."
T46	Quotation 5866 5895	"Kiss? What do you kiss for?"
T47	Quotation 5896 5953	"Why, that, you know, is to-- well, they always do that."
T48	Quotation 5954 5966	"Everybody?"
T49	Quotation 5967 6063	"Why, yes, everybody that's in love with each other. Do you remember what I wrote on the slate?"
T50	Quotation 6064 6075	"Ye-- yes."
T51	Quotation 6076 6090	"What was it?"
T52	Quotation 6091 6112	"I sha'n't tell you."
T53	Quotation 6113 6132	"Shall I tell YOU?"
T54	Quotation 6133 6166	"Ye-- yes-- but some other time."
T55	Quotation 6167 6177	"No, now."
T56	Quotation 6178 6204	"No, not now-- to-morrow."
T57	Quotation 6205 6282	"Oh, no, NOW. Please, Becky-- I'll whisper it, I'll whisper it ever so easy."
