T238	Quotation 29287 29308	"I! I never done it!"
T239	Quotation 29309 29351	"Look here! That kind of talk won't wash."
R301	Addressee Arg1:T232 Arg2:T238	
R302	Speaker Arg1:T236 Arg2:T238	
R303	Addressee Arg1:T236 Arg2:T239	
R304	Speaker Arg1:T232 Arg2:T239	
T240	Quotation 29384 29761	"I thought I'd got sober. I'd no business to drink to-night. But it's in my head yet-- worse'n when we started here. I'm all in a muddle; can't recollect anything of it, hardly. Tell me, Joe-- HONEST, now, old feller-- did I do it? Joe, I never meant to-- 'pon my soul and honor, I never meant to, Joe. Tell me how it was, Joe. Oh, it's awful-- and him so young and promising."
R305	Addressee Arg1:T236 Arg2:T240	
T241	Quotation 29762 30048	"Why, you two was scuffling, and he fetched you one with the headboard and you fell flat; and then up you come, all reeling and staggering like, and snatched the knife and jammed it into him, just as he fetched you another awful clip-- and here you've laid, as dead as a wedge til now."
R306	Speaker Arg1:T236 Arg2:T241	
T242	Entity 29352 29358	Potter
R307	Speaker Arg1:T242 Arg2:T240	
R308	Addressee Arg1:T242 Arg2:T241	
T243	Quotation 30049 30467	"Oh, I didn't know what I was a-doing. I wish I may die this minute if I did. It was all on account of the whiskey and the excitement, I reckon. I never used a weepon in my life before, Joe. I've fought, but never with weepons. They'll all say that. Joe, don't tell! Say you won't tell, Joe-- that's a good feller. I always liked you, Joe, and stood up for you, too. Don't you remember? You WON'T tell, WILL you, Joe?"
R309	Speaker Arg1:T242 Arg2:T243	
R310	Addressee Arg1:T236 Arg2:T243	
T244	Quotation 30572 30707	"No, you've always been fair and square with me, Muff Potter, and I won't go back on you. There, now, that's as fair as a man can say."
T245	Quotation 30708 30783	"Oh, Joe, you're an angel. I'll bless you for this the longest day I live."
T246	Entity 30788 30794	Potter
T247	Quotation 30809 30970	"Come, now, that's enough of that. This ain't any time for blubbering. You be off yonder way and I'll go this. Move, now, and don't leave any tracks behind you."
R311	Addressee Arg1:T246 Arg2:T244	
R312	Speaker Arg1:T246 Arg2:T245	
R313	Addressee Arg1:T246 Arg2:T247	
T248	Entity 31029 31043	The half-breed
