T631	Quotation 87500 87532	"What makes the candle blow so?"
T632	Cue 87533 87537	said
T633	Entity 87538 87548	Aunt Polly
R784	Cueing Arg1:T632 Arg2:T631	
R785	Speaker Arg1:T633 Arg2:T631	
T634	Quotation 87566 87680	"Why, that door's open, I believe. Why, of course it is. No end of strange things now. Go 'long and shut it, Sid."
R786	Speaker Arg1:T633 Arg2:T634	
T635	Entity 87094 87097	Sid
R787	Addressee Arg1:T635 Arg2:T634	
T636	Quotation 87830 87852	"But as I was saying,"
T637	Cue 87853 87857	said
T638	Entity 87858 87868	Aunt Polly
T639	Quotation 87870 88076	"he warn't BAD, so to say --only mischEEvous. Only just giddy, and harum-scarum, you know. He warn't any more responsible than a colt. HE never meant any harm, and he was the best-hearted boy that ever was"
R788	Cueing Arg1:T637 Arg2:T636	
R789	Speaker Arg1:T638 Arg2:T636	
R790	Cueing Arg1:T637 Arg2:T639	
R791	Speaker Arg1:T638 Arg2:T639	
T640	Quotation 88101 88480	"It was just so with my Joe-- always full of his devilment, and up to every kind of mischief, but he was just as unselfish and kind as he could be-- and laws bless me, to think I went and whipped him for taking that cream, never once recollecting that I throwed it out myself because it was sour, and I never to see him again in this world, never, never, never, poor abused boy!"
T641	Entity 88485 88496	Mrs. Harper
R792	Addressee Arg1:T641 Arg2:T636	
R793	Addressee Arg1:T641 Arg2:T639	
R794	Speaker Arg1:T641 Arg2:T640	
R795	Addressee Arg1:T638 Arg2:T640	
T642	Quotation 88533 88571	"I hope Tom's better off where he is,"
T643	Cue 88572 88576	said
T644	Entity 88577 88580	Sid
T645	Quotation 88582 88624	"but if he'd been better in some ways -- "
R796	Cueing Arg1:T643 Arg2:T642	
R797	Speaker Arg1:T644 Arg2:T642	
R798	Cueing Arg1:T643 Arg2:T645	
R799	Speaker Arg1:T644 Arg2:T645	
