R801	Addressee Arg1:T646 Arg2:T645	
T647	Quotation 88625 88631	"SID!"
T648	Entity 88654 88668	the old lady's
T649	Quotation 88702 88974	"Not a word against my Tom, now that he's gone! God'll take care of HIM-- never you trouble YOURself, sir! Oh, Mrs. Harper, I don't know how to give him up! I don't know how to give him up! He was such a comfort to me, although he tormented my old heart out of me, 'most."
R802	Speaker Arg1:T648 Arg2:T647	
R803	Speaker Arg1:T648 Arg2:T649	
R804	Addressee Arg1:T644 Arg2:T647	
R805	Addressee Arg1:T644 Arg2:T649	
R806	Addressee Arg1:T641 Arg2:T649	
T650	Quotation 88975 89289	"The Lord giveth and the Lord hath taken away-- Blessed be the name of the Lord! But it's so hard-- Oh, it's so hard! Only last Saturday my Joe busted a firecracker right under my nose and I knocked him sprawling. Little did I know then, how soon-- Oh, if it was to do over again I'd hug him and bless him for it."
R807	Speaker Arg1:T641 Arg2:T650	
R808	Addressee Arg1:T648 Arg2:T650	
T651	Quotation 89290 89701	"Yes, yes, yes, I know just how you feel, Mrs. Harper, I know just exactly how you feel. No longer ago than yesterday noon, my Tom took and filled the cat full of Pain-killer, and I did think the cretur would tear the house down. And God forgive me, I cracked Tom's head with my thimble, poor boy, poor dead boy. But he's out of all his troubles now. And the last words I ever heard him say was to reproach -- "
T652	Entity 89735 89747	the old lady
R809	Speaker Arg1:T652 Arg2:T651	
R810	Addressee Arg1:T641 Arg2:T651	
T653	Entity 93739 93742	Joe
T654	Cue 93743 93746	say
T655	Quotation 93748 93955	"No, Tom's true-blue, Huck, and he'll come back. He won't desert. He knows that would be a disgrace to a pirate, and Tom's too proud for that sort of thing. He's up to something or other. Now I wonder what?"
R811	Speaker Arg1:T653 Arg2:T655	
R812	Cueing Arg1:T654 Arg2:T655	
T656	Quotation 93956 94003	"Well, the things is ours, anyway, ain't they?"
T657	Quotation 94004 94099	"Pretty near, but not yet, Huck. The writing says they are if he ain't back here to breakfast."
R813	Speaker Arg1:T653 Arg2:T657	
T658	Quotation 94100 94114	"Which he is!"
T659	Cue 94115 94124	exclaimed
T660	Entity 94125 94128	Tom
R814	Cueing Arg1:T659 Arg2:T658	
R815	Speaker Arg1:T660 Arg2:T658	
R816	Addressee Arg1:T653 Arg2:T658	
T661	Entity 97503 97505	He
T662	Cue 97506 97510	said
T663	Quotation 97547 97739	"I bet there's been pirates on this island before, boys. We'll explore it again. They've hid treasures here somewhere. How'd you feel to light on a rotten chest full of gold and silver-- hey?"
R817	Speaker Arg1:T661 Arg2:T663	
R818	Cueing Arg1:T662 Arg2:T663	
T664	Entity 97285 97289	Huck
R819	Addressee Arg1:T664 Arg2:T663	
T665	Entity 97896 97899	Joe
