R981	Addressee Arg1:T799 Arg2:T800	
R982	Addressee Arg1:T799 Arg2:T803	
T804	Quotation 119645 119662	"Would you, Tom?"
T805	Cue 119663 119667	said
T806	Entity 119668 119678	Aunt Polly
R983	Cueing Arg1:T805 Arg2:T804	
R984	Speaker Arg1:T806 Arg2:T804	
T807	Quotation 119709 119755	"Say, now, would you, if you'd thought of it?"
R985	Cueing Arg1:T805 Arg2:T807	
R986	Speaker Arg1:T806 Arg2:T807	
R987	Addressee Arg1:T799 Arg2:T804	
R988	Addressee Arg1:T799 Arg2:T807	
T808	Quotation 119756 119813	"I-- well, I don't know. 'Twould 'a' spoiled everything."
R989	Addressee Arg1:T806 Arg2:T808	
R990	Speaker Arg1:T799 Arg2:T808	
T809	Quotation 119814 119852	"Tom, I hoped you loved me that much,"
T810	Cue 119853 119857	said
T811	Entity 119858 119868	Aunt Polly
R991	Cueing Arg1:T810 Arg2:T809	
R992	Speaker Arg1:T811 Arg2:T809	
T812	Entity 119908 119915	the boy
T813	Quotation 119917 120011	"It would have been something if you'd cared enough to THINK of it, even if you didn't DO it."
