R1014	Addressee Arg1:T811 Arg2:T823	
R1015	Addressee Arg1:T811 Arg2:T826	
T827	Quotation 120595 120686	"It ain't much -- a cat does that much-- but it's better than nothing. What did you dream?"
R1016	Addressee Arg1:T825 Arg2:T827	
R1017	Speaker Arg1:T811 Arg2:T827	
T828	Quotation 120687 120820	"Why, Wednesday night I dreamt that you was sitting over there by the bed, and Sid was sitting by the woodbox, and Mary next to him."
R1018	Speaker Arg1:T825 Arg2:T828	
R1019	Addressee Arg1:T811 Arg2:T828	
T829	Quotation 120821 120921	"Well, so we did. So we always do. I'm glad your dreams could take even that much trouble about us."
R1020	Addressee Arg1:T825 Arg2:T829	
R1021	Speaker Arg1:T811 Arg2:T829	
T830	Quotation 120922 120971	"And I dreamt that Joe Harper's mother was here."
T831	Quotation 120972 121016	"Why, she was here! Did you dream any more?"
T832	Quotation 121017 121050	"Oh, lots. But it's so dim, now."
T833	Quotation 121051 121088	"Well, try to recollect-- can't you?"
T834	Quotation 121089 121159	"Somehow it seems to me that the wind-- the wind blowed the-- the -- "
T835	Quotation 121160 121213	"Try harder, Tom! The wind did blow something. Come!"
T836	Entity 121214 121217	Tom
T837	Cue 121282 121286	said
