R1037	Speaker Arg1:T836 Arg2:T840	
T841	Quotation 121452 121465	"Go ON, Tom!"
T842	Quotation 121466 121562	"Just let me study a moment-- just a moment. Oh, yes-- you said you believed the door was open."
T843	Quotation 121563 121615	"As I'm sitting here, I did! Didn't I, Mary! Go on!"
T844	Quotation 121616 121718	"And then-- and then-- well I won't be certain, but it seems like as if you made Sid go and-- and -- "
T845	Quotation 121719 121785	"Well? Well? What did I make him do, Tom? What did I make him do?"
T846	Quotation 121786 121834	"You made him-- you-- Oh, you made him shut it."
T847	Quotation 121835 122110	"Well, for the land's sake! I never heard the beat of that in all my days! Don't tell ME there ain't anything in dreams, any more. Sereny Harper shall know of this before I'm an hour older. I'd like to see her get around THIS with her rubbage 'bout superstition. Go on, Tom!"
T848	Quotation 122111 122305	"Oh, it's all getting just as bright as day, now. Next you said I warn't BAD, only mischeevous and harum-scarum, and not any more responsible than-- than -- I think it was a colt, or something."
T849	Quotation 122306 122359	"And so it was! Well, goodness gracious! Go on, Tom!"
T850	Quotation 122360 122388	"And then you began to cry."
T851	Quotation 122389 122452	"So I did. So I did. Not the first time, neither. And then -- "
T852	Quotation 122453 122619	"Then Mrs. Harper she began to cry, and said Joe was just the same, and she wished she hadn't whipped him for taking cream when she'd throwed it out her own self -- "
T853	Quotation 122620 122727	"Tom! The sperrit was upon you! You was a prophesying-- that's what you was doing! Land alive, go on, Tom!"
T854	Quotation 122728 122760	"Then Sid he said-- he said -- "
